========================
RAII / atomicity verification:
========================

DashMap v6 `Entry::Occupied` and `Entry::Vacant` both hold the
shard write-lock for `path`'s shard. `Entry::Vacant::insert` stores
the built table under the same write-lock before the `Entry` guard
drops. Any concurrent `entry(path)` from another thread blocks on
the shard lock and observes `Entry::Occupied` after the first
thread returns. The `.entry()` guard also dropping on panic inside
the closure (pre-insert) leaves the map unchanged — standard RAII
behaviour per the DashMap docs. `Entry::Vacant::insert` itself is
panic-free for our use (allocating a `SymbolTable<C,L>` and
inserting pre-cloned entries into its internal `HashMap`).

========================
Observations from the post-fix dump:
========================

1. The pre-fix signature (t1 overwriting t2's populated
   helper table) is fully GONE: the `Created` emission is singular
   on `helper`.

2. The ordering "Created → AlreadyPresent" always holds:
   ts=20007333 (Created) precedes ts=20016083 and ts=20024500 (both
   AlreadyPresent). Never a post-Created re-Created.

3. `helper-val` lookup at ts=20800583
   (`RegisterImportsLookup module=helper`) succeeds — no
   `'helper-val' not found` error, no retry.

4. The observability tag distinguishes the outcome without a new
   payload variant — the existing `state` field on `Module` is
   overloaded for the `SymbolTableEnsure` tag (0=Created,
   1=AlreadyPresent) and rendered symbolically by
   `format_event_line`. This keeps the scheduler trace's
   on-the-wire format and its unit-test surface stable.

5. Some `SymbolTableEnsure` emissions on `primitives` / `user` /
   `prelude` repeat `AlreadyPresent` multiple times during
   session bootstrap — expected, since those modules are ensured
   by many internal code paths during builtin registration
   (`register_builtins` and its callees) as well as REPL setup.
   None constitute a race window; they are all serialised on the
   main thread during startup.

